# Git Merge Conflict Resolution Lab
## Verify Repository Status
```bash
git status
```
---
## Create a New Branch
```bash
git branch GitWork
git checkout GitWork
```
---
## Create hello.xml
```bash
echo "<message>Hello from GitWork</message>" > hello.xml
```
Check the status:
```bash
git status
```
---
## Commit Changes
```bash
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Added hello.xml in GitWork"
```
---
## Switch to Master
``bash
git checkout master
```
or
```bash
git checkout main
```
---
## Create hello.xml with Different Content
```bash
echo "<message>Hello from Master</message>" > hello.xml
```
Check the status:
```bash
git status
```
Commit the changes:
```bash
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Added hello.xml in master"
```
---
## View Commit History
```bash
git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all
```
---
## Compare Branches
```bash
git diff master GitWork
```
or
```bash
git diff main GitWork
```
---
## Merge Branch
```bash
git merge GitWork
```
If a merge conflict occurs, open **hello.xml** and remove the conflict markers:
```text
<<<<<<< HEAD
Master Content
GitWork Content
>>>>>>> GitWork
```
Edit the file with the required content and save it.
---

## Complete Conflict Resolution

```bash
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Resolved merge conflict"
```
---
## Ignore Backup Files
Open `.gitignore`
```bash
notepad .gitignore
```
Add:
```text
*.bak
```
Save the file.
Commit the changes:
```bash
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Updated .gitignore"
```
---
## View Branches
```bash
git branch
```
---
## Delete Merged Branch
```bash
git branch -d GitWork
```
---
## View Final Log
```bash
git log --oneline --graph --decorate
```
---
## Commands Used
```bash
git status
git branch GitWork
git checkout GitWork
echo "<message>Hello from GitWork</message>" > hello.xml
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Added hello.xml in GitWork"
git checkout master
echo "<message>Hello from Master</message>" > hello.xml
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Added hello.xml in master"
git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all
git diff master GitWork
git merge GitWork
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Resolved merge conflict"
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Updated .gitignore"
git branch
git branch -d GitWork
git log --oneline --graph --decorate
```
## Result
- Verified repository status.
- Created the **GitWork** branch.
- Added and modified **hello.xml** in both branches.
- Merged the branch into **master**.
- Resolved the merge conflict successfully.
- Updated the **.gitignore** file.
- Deleted the merged branch.
- Verified the final commit history.
